<title>POLAND: Warsaw bourse opposes dual listings with OTC mkt.</title>
<headline>Warsaw bourse opposes dual listings with OTC mkt.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The supervisory and management boards of the Warsaw Stock Exchange oppose the listing of a firm's shares on the bourse and Poland's nascent over the counter market, the bourse's deputy president said.</p>
<p>&quot;We think it's inadvisable -- our market is too small and such a spreading of shares makes it not known which price is more true,&quot; Ryszard Czerniawski told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>But he said the bourse's opinion was not legally binding and was just a guideline for issuers.</p>
<p>Currently insurer Polisa has some of its shares on the bourse's main market, others on CeTO, the OTC market.</p>
<p>On Thursday the stock closed at 7.5 zlotys on the bourse and traded at between 6.4 and 7.3 zlotys on CeTO.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
